{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"False-positive evidence for operator dismissal (no GitHub writes made by the agent). Source of each flow: SARIF of CodeQL analysis 2088549160 (commit 7ea86184, refs/heads/main).\n\n**#91** py/clear-text-logging-sensitive-data, src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py:457 (`rebar llm setup --output json`). CodeQL source: dict keys `anthropic_api_key` / `openai_api_key` in the `report` dict (line 445-448), matched by the name heuristic `api.?key`. Actual value: `rebar.llm.config.available_backends()` sets both to `bool(os.environ.get(...))`, so only True/False reaches stdout. No key material flows. Suggested dismissal reason: false positive — presence booleans, not key values. A code-side fix would require renaming fields in the JSON output contract.\n\n**#93** py/incomplete-url-substring-sanitization, tests/unit/test_uv_pin_guard.py:232. `result.stderr` is the diagnostic text of scripts/check_uv_pin.py; the test asserts the message names the forbidden token `raw.githubusercontent.com` (from `FORBIDDEN_ACTION_TEXT`), after appending that token as a comment to the action file. No URL is parsed, trusted, or allowed by this check. Suggested reason: false positive / used in tests — diagnostic-text assertion, not URL sanitization.\n\n**#94** py/clear-text-logging-sensitive-data, src/rebar/_config_coercion.py:91. The sink logs an unknown `[llm]` config KEY NAME. All 4 CodeQL flows start at test fixtures (tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_auth_introspection.py:26 and test_mcp_auth_proxy.py:24, a `SECRET_ENV` string that is an environment-variable NAME) under the `mcp` section, then reach `_warn_unknown_llm_keys` via `coerce_sparse`'s `for sect, val in raw.items()` loop, ignoring the `if sect == \"llm\"` guard, and treat a dict value as the iterated key (`leftover [Tuple element at index 1]` -> `key`). The logged value is never a config value. Suggested reason: false positive — logs key names only; source is test data.\n\nTrue positives #89, #90 (workflow lint value previews) and #92 (acli host substring check) are fixed in code under this ticket."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793755026925849001,"uuid":"1a5529fc-427e-484b-8d9b-9c7cea291065"}